module gunbc.plans.language_target_self_host_frontier


fn language_target_self_host_frontier_body() -> List<std.markdown.MarkdownBlock> {
  [
    gunbc.plans.md_helpers.p(text: "**Status:** staging map, captured pre-un-shelve. The multi-language self-host lane is §4-shelved (ROADMAP: \"TypeScript first-class emit + TS self-host … resumes after the Rust fixed point\"). This map exists so the lane can be **staffed continuously** the moment it un-shelves: every dependency is understood from beginning to end, Rust is the model, and the exotic languages are placed as deliberate stresses on it. `solve` is resolved as **not a substrate change** — see [solve-higher-order-design.md](solve-higher-order-design.md)."),
    gunbc.plans.md_helpers.p(text: "**Governing invariant (the anti-hack guarantee):** every target ends in exactly one of two *declared* states — **green-by-execution at a named bar**, or a **typed frontier row** (`bar reached · reason · dissolution trigger`). No silent `body_lexeme: String` anemic leaves, no orphan un-enrolled smokes, no anchor-stub masquerading as a finished target. \"Done\" and \"refused-with-reason\" are the only terminal states. This is the §7 typed self-host frontier applied to every target at once."),
    gunbc.plans.md_helpers.p(text: "**Not yet built (declared gap, un-shelve-scale — DO NOT pretend present):** the typed `LanguageTargetFrontierRow` carrier that would make each row below *machine-checked* — plus its completeness lens and per-row RED witnesses — **does not exist today**. This table is the interim prose ledger. **Enrollment trigger** = lane un-shelve → author the carrier + witnesses. It is recorded here as a gap, not claimed as present machinery."),
    gunbc.plans.md_helpers.p(text: "**Offline / on-demand smokes (honest exception to \"no orphan un-enrolled smokes\"):** the C and Rust F5 emit-vs-eval witnesses live under `test/claim/execution/`, which is in `witness_exclusion_substrings` (`ci_layer_roots.dag`), so they are **excluded from discovery and un-enrolled** in per-PR CI. They are labeled **OFFLINE** — run offline / on-demand — with a **named enrollment trigger = lane un-shelve** (un-shelve → move them out of the exclusion set / enroll). They are NOT claimed as enrolled."),
    gunbc.plans.md_helpers.p(text: "Bars: **(a)** grammar-inverse translation rows on the committed TargetModel · **(b)** emit witness produces the expected source · **(c)** a real toolchain runs the output green-by-execution through the *typed* `run_emit_host` transport · **self-host** the target emits the compiler's own sources, behaviorally equivalent (§7)."),
    gunbc.plans.md_helpers.hr(),
    gunbc.plans.md_helpers.h2(text: "Two orthogonal stress axes"),
    gunbc.plans.md_helpers.p(text: "The whole point of exotic-first is that the curly-brace family *confirms* the design while the exotics *falsify* it. There are two independent things to falsify:"),
    gunbc.plans.md_helpers.ul(items: [
      gunbc.plans.md_helpers.li(text: "**Emit-generality axis** — does \"one grammar read backwards\" reach targets whose computational model is *not* imperative-forward? Stressed hardest by: **Verilog** (concurrent / clock-stepped), **SPICE** (continuous-time / ODE), **LLVM-IR** (SSA / no runtime). If emit generalizes here, the \"medium-agnostic, one grammar N directions\" claim (§4) is real."),
      gunbc.plans.md_helpers.li(text: "**Self-host axis** — does the seed-shrink story (§7) hold in a *second* language, or is it secretly Rust-shaped? Stressed by generalizing the self-host frontier runner past Rust to a second runnable language. (Reality check: Rust itself is **not yet self-hosted** — see the F5 / rust rows below.)"),
    ]),
    gunbc.plans.md_helpers.p(text: "**The emit-only family can only stress the first axis** (you cannot run a compiler as a circuit or as bare SSA). The runnable family stresses both. Keeping these axes separate is what keeps the lane honest about what each language *proves*."),
    gunbc.plans.md_helpers.hr(),
    gunbc.plans.md_helpers.h2(text: "Shared foundation (Rust-built; the front-loaded cost — partly still owed)"),
    std.markdown.TableBlock {
      header: gunbc.plans.md_helpers.row(cells: [gunbc.plans.md_helpers.cell(text: "id"), gunbc.plans.md_helpers.cell(text: "foundation"), gunbc.plans.md_helpers.cell(text: "state")]),
      alignments: [std.markdown.AlignNone, std.markdown.AlignNone, std.markdown.AlignNone],
      rows: [
        gunbc.plans.md_helpers.row(cells: [gunbc.plans.md_helpers.cell(text: "**F0**"), gunbc.plans.md_helpers.cell(text: "`emit` / `emit_module` pipeline (walks TargetModel edges backward; new target = rows, no pipeline edit)"), gunbc.plans.md_helpers.cell(text: "✓ done")]),
        gunbc.plans.md_helpers.row(cells: [gunbc.plans.md_helpers.cell(text: "**F1**"), gunbc.plans.md_helpers.cell(text: "`TargetModel` 4-edge + grammar-inverse translation rows"), gunbc.plans.md_helpers.cell(text: "✓ done")]),
        gunbc.plans.md_helpers.row(cells: [gunbc.plans.md_helpers.cell(text: "**F2**"), gunbc.plans.md_helpers.cell(text: "VEP (`TargetValueExpressionProjection`) — the general body producer"), gunbc.plans.md_helpers.cell(text: "**partial** (rust: `^rust_token_unwired_\{else,loop,match,fat_arrow\}`, `v2.extdeps.languages.rust` `rust_value_expression_projection`) · partial (TS: match/loop/bind-in unwired) · **absent** (python, ecmascript)")]),
        gunbc.plans.md_helpers.row(cells: [gunbc.plans.md_helpers.cell(text: "**F3**"), gunbc.plans.md_helpers.cell(text: "`BlockEvaluationMode` statement spine (`ValueProducing` vs `StatementSequenced`)"), gunbc.plans.md_helpers.cell(text: "✓ type exists; TS's `StatementSequenced` arm produces the correct fail-closed refusals")]),
        gunbc.plans.md_helpers.row(cells: [gunbc.plans.md_helpers.cell(text: "**F4**"), gunbc.plans.md_helpers.cell(text: "`ProcessProgram` transport + `run_emit_host`; executable identity **bound per extdeps transport row** (`v2.std.host_transport` `HostTransportDescriptor` / `ProcessProgram`), compiler dispatch **generic** (`v2.compiler.emit_host` `process_program_name`)"), gunbc.plans.md_helpers.cell(text: "✓ done — `HostToolProgram.executable` is carried by the row and generic dispatch returns that value; target-specific work is only to configure a runtime row where one is absent")]),
        gunbc.plans.md_helpers.row(cells: [gunbc.plans.md_helpers.cell(text: "**F5**"), gunbc.plans.md_helpers.cell(text: "self-host frontier runner (`v2.compiler.emit_host` `run_test_claim_module_emit_vs_eval`: emit → build → run → compare-to-eval)"), gunbc.plans.md_helpers.cell(text: "✓ machinery **for Rust only**, run **OFFLINE** (excluded from discovery). Rust is **not** self-hosted, and after the roster cut there is **no symbol that counts this** — `compiler_frontier_emitter_produced_count` is deleted and nothing replaced it, so the bar is stated qualitatively on purpose: **no module carries a producer-qualified promotion.** The surviving authority is `v2.compiler.self_host.emitter_producer_provenance`, which holds the producer facts as structure rather than as a tally — `EmitterProducer` x `EmissionQualification`, `mint_producer_emission_receipt` as the only route to a receipt, and the realized-closure wall (`seed_emit_rust_reachable`) under which a `V2Emitter*` mint is unwritable while `v1.compiler.emit_rust` is in the closure. Re-deriving a count is a future obligation, not a present fact.")]),
        gunbc.plans.md_helpers.row(cells: [gunbc.plans.md_helpers.cell(text: "**F6**"), gunbc.plans.md_helpers.cell(text: "`solve` — **structural** = existing `solve_constraints` / `ConstraintGraph` authority (extend, no fork); **numerical** = *absent* typed gap (finite measure + `TerminationProof`, typed residual-acceptance contract, extdeps solver handler)"), gunbc.plans.md_helpers.cell(text: "**off critical path** — not needed for emit-to-simulator; see solve doc")]),
        gunbc.plans.md_helpers.row(cells: [gunbc.plans.md_helpers.cell(text: "**F7**"), gunbc.plans.md_helpers.cell(text: "declaration emission generic over target (`v2.compiler.emit_semantic_decl` `emit_semantic_type_decl`)"), gunbc.plans.md_helpers.cell(text: "✓ done — the declaration emitter accepts a `TargetModel` and reads its emission bundle through `v2.std.compilers.semantic_decl_emission` `semantic_decl_emission_from_target`")]),
      ],
    },
    gunbc.plans.md_helpers.h3(text: "The highest-leverage shared dependencies (do these once, everyone inherits)"),
    gunbc.plans.md_helpers.ol(items: [
      gunbc.plans.md_helpers.li(text: "**F2 VEP completion** — wire the unwired forms **once** (rust's `^rust_token_unwired_\{else,loop,match,fat_arrow\}`; TS's match / loop / bind-in) in the `StatementSequenced` arm; the family inherits body breadth. Python additionally needs its *first* VEP edge."),
    ]),
    gunbc.plans.md_helpers.hr(),
    gunbc.plans.md_helpers.h2(text: "Per-target frontier table (grounded from the typed census, 2026-07-15)"),
    std.markdown.TableBlock {
      header: gunbc.plans.md_helpers.row(cells: [gunbc.plans.md_helpers.cell(text: "target"), gunbc.plans.md_helpers.cell(text: "family"), gunbc.plans.md_helpers.cell(text: "current bar (verified)"), gunbc.plans.md_helpers.cell(text: "honest end-state"), gunbc.plans.md_helpers.cell(text: "key deps"), gunbc.plans.md_helpers.cell(text: "stress axis")]),
      alignments: [std.markdown.AlignNone, std.markdown.AlignNone, std.markdown.AlignNone, std.markdown.AlignNone, std.markdown.AlignNone, std.markdown.AlignNone],
      rows: [
        gunbc.plans.md_helpers.row(cells: [gunbc.plans.md_helpers.cell(text: "**rust**"), gunbc.plans.md_helpers.cell(text: "compiled"), gunbc.plans.md_helpers.cell(text: "compiled; bar-c; F2 **partial** (`^rust_token_unwired_\{else,loop,match,fat_arrow\}`, `v2.extdeps.languages.rust` `rust_value_expression_projection`); F5 emit-vs-eval fixture **OFFLINE**"), gunbc.plans.md_helpers.cell(text: "**zero producer-qualified emissions, and no roster to count them against** — the 27-row `SeedRetained` roster is DELETED, so this cell no longer has a denominator and does not invent one. `v2.compiler.self_host.emitter_producer_provenance` `mint_producer_emission_receipt` is the only route to a producer-qualified receipt and no v2-emitter-produced promotion exists; behavioral-equivalence standing is carried by `BehavioralProbeBinding`, whose `BehavioralProbeUnbound` arm is the honest state for a receipt that has produced source and nothing more. Reference model, **NOT self-hosted**"), gunbc.plans.md_helpers.cell(text: "F2 completion; F5 self-host generalization"), gunbc.plans.md_helpers.cell(text: "(reference model)")]),
        gunbc.plans.md_helpers.row(cells: [gunbc.plans.md_helpers.cell(text: "**cpp — Phase-0-C**"), gunbc.plans.md_helpers.cell(text: "compiled"), gunbc.plans.md_helpers.cell(text: "bar-c via `cc`, proven by an **OFFLINE** witness in `test/claim/execution/` (excluded from discovery)"), gunbc.plans.md_helpers.cell(text: "bar-c green (offline); self-host N/A at this phase"), gunbc.plans.md_helpers.cell(text: "F5-generalize"), gunbc.plans.md_helpers.cell(text: "(confirms)")]),
        gunbc.plans.md_helpers.row(cells: [gunbc.plans.md_helpers.cell(text: "**cpp — full C target**"), gunbc.plans.md_helpers.cell(text: "compiled"), gunbc.plans.md_helpers.cell(text: "**below bar-a** for full C"), gunbc.plans.md_helpers.cell(text: "blocked — needs **monomorphization** (grep-**zero** in tree), **closure conversion**, a **discriminant-tag row kind**, **multi-file (header/impl) projection**, and **ABI/linkage** — none present"), gunbc.plans.md_helpers.cell(text: "monomorphization, closure conversion, tag-row kind, multi-file projection, ABI/linkage"), gunbc.plans.md_helpers.cell(text: "(confirms — hard)")]),
        gunbc.plans.md_helpers.row(cells: [gunbc.plans.md_helpers.cell(text: "**go**"), gunbc.plans.md_helpers.cell(text: "compiled"), gunbc.plans.md_helpers.cell(text: "**skeleton** — needs TargetModel buildout"), gunbc.plans.md_helpers.cell(text: "**self-host** (first non-rust self-host — the F5 generalization proof), once built"), gunbc.plans.md_helpers.cell(text: "TargetModel buildout, surface spellings, F5"), gunbc.plans.md_helpers.cell(text: "**self-host axis**")]),
        gunbc.plans.md_helpers.row(cells: [gunbc.plans.md_helpers.cell(text: "**java / kotlin / swift**"), gunbc.plans.md_helpers.cell(text: "compiled"), gunbc.plans.md_helpers.cell(text: "**skeleton** — need TargetModel buildout"), gunbc.plans.md_helpers.cell(text: "bar-c → self-host"), gunbc.plans.md_helpers.cell(text: "TargetModel buildout, runtime-row configuration, spellings, inherit F2/F3/F5"), gunbc.plans.md_helpers.cell(text: "(confirms — parallel)")]),
        gunbc.plans.md_helpers.row(cells: [gunbc.plans.md_helpers.cell(text: "**typescript**"), gunbc.plans.md_helpers.cell(text: "interpreted"), gunbc.plans.md_helpers.cell(text: "F2 **partial** (match/loop/bind-in unwired); runtime row is configured (`v2.extdeps.languages.typescript` `ts_runtime_row`), but this pre-un-shelve map does not establish current bar-c execution"), gunbc.plans.md_helpers.cell(text: "self-host"), gunbc.plans.md_helpers.cell(text: "F2 completion (match/loop/bind-in), operator catalog"), gunbc.plans.md_helpers.cell(text: "self-host axis")]),
        gunbc.plans.md_helpers.row(cells: [gunbc.plans.md_helpers.cell(text: "**python**"), gunbc.plans.md_helpers.cell(text: "interpreted"), gunbc.plans.md_helpers.cell(text: "**no VEP edge — add-only**"), gunbc.plans.md_helpers.cell(text: "bar-c → self-host"), gunbc.plans.md_helpers.cell(text: "F2 *first* edge, operator catalog"), gunbc.plans.md_helpers.cell(text: "self-host axis")]),
        gunbc.plans.md_helpers.row(cells: [gunbc.plans.md_helpers.cell(text: "**ecmascript**"), gunbc.plans.md_helpers.cell(text: "interpreted"), gunbc.plans.md_helpers.cell(text: "**orphan (0 consumers)**"), gunbc.plans.md_helpers.cell(text: "**decide first**: adopt as TS's JS base, or delete"), gunbc.plans.md_helpers.cell(text: "(adoption decision)"), gunbc.plans.md_helpers.cell(text: "—")]),
        gunbc.plans.md_helpers.row(cells: [gunbc.plans.md_helpers.cell(text: "**lean**"), gunbc.plans.md_helpers.cell(text: "expression/ML"), gunbc.plans.md_helpers.cell(text: "**below bar-a** — type model + anchor test only, **no committed TargetModel** (0 `target_model` / `translation_rules_node` refs)"), gunbc.plans.md_helpers.cell(text: "self-host on an *expression* spine (not statement), once a TargetModel is built"), gunbc.plans.md_helpers.cell(text: "committed TargetModel, F3 generalization (expression-mode), F2, F5"), gunbc.plans.md_helpers.cell(text: "self-host axis (spine falsifier)")]),
        gunbc.plans.md_helpers.row(cells: [gunbc.plans.md_helpers.cell(text: "**verilog**"), gunbc.plans.md_helpers.cell(text: "HDL"), gunbc.plans.md_helpers.cell(text: "**committed TargetModel landed** (`v2.extdeps.languages.verilog` `verilog_target_model_for`) and a first module emitted through the generic fold from language-neutral intent; **Icarus Verilog compiled and simulated the emitted bytes** — the four-row interlock truth table is a recorded run (`product.compute_board.simulation_receipt` `interlock_verilog_run`), joined to today's emission by an enrolled witness. Residue: the emitted profile is combinational module/port/assign only, and nothing re-executes the simulator on a cadence"), gunbc.plans.md_helpers.cell(text: "**bar-c green + frontier row `self-host: N/A (hardware)`**"), gunbc.plans.md_helpers.cell(text: "widen the emitted profile past combinational assign; a cadence that re-runs the recorded simulations rather than joining to a one-time observation"), gunbc.plans.md_helpers.cell(text: "**emit-generality (concurrent)**")]),
        gunbc.plans.md_helpers.row(cells: [gunbc.plans.md_helpers.cell(text: "**spice**"), gunbc.plans.md_helpers.cell(text: "analog format"), gunbc.plans.md_helpers.cell(text: "**ngspice has now run the emitted deck** — the operating point of the emitted conditioning network is a recorded run (`product.compute_board.simulation_receipt` `conditioning_network_run`) whose 1.2 mA source current discriminates the `k` scale suffix a bare magnitude would have lost; the golden comparison remains beside it. The product-local SPICE printer is deleted and `v2.extdeps.formats.spice` owns every byte"), gunbc.plans.md_helpers.cell(text: "bar-c green + frontier row `self-host: N/A (analog)`. **No Modelica carrier in-tree** — dual-emit is future, not present"), gunbc.plans.md_helpers.cell(text: "a cadence that re-runs the recorded simulation rather than joining to a one-time observation; Modelica carrier does not yet exist"), gunbc.plans.md_helpers.cell(text: "**emit-generality (continuous)**")]),
        gunbc.plans.md_helpers.row(cells: [gunbc.plans.md_helpers.cell(text: "**llvm_ir**"), gunbc.plans.md_helpers.cell(text: "IR/backend"), gunbc.plans.md_helpers.cell(text: "**below bar-a** — type model + anchor, **no committed TargetModel** (0 `target_model` / `translation_rules_node` refs)"), gunbc.plans.md_helpers.cell(text: "bar-c green + frontier row `self-host: N/A (no runtime)` — the Rust/cargo-free lowering path, once a TargetModel is built"), gunbc.plans.md_helpers.cell(text: "committed TargetModel, configure the `llc`/`clang` runtime row"), gunbc.plans.md_helpers.cell(text: "**emit-generality (SSA)**")]),
        gunbc.plans.md_helpers.row(cells: [gunbc.plans.md_helpers.cell(text: "**wasm**"), gunbc.plans.md_helpers.cell(text: "IR/backend"), gunbc.plans.md_helpers.cell(text: "has a **TargetModel** (bundle/lex/binding_spellings) BUT **bar-c unreachable** — `runtime_row: target_emit_host_runtime_row_unconfigured` (`v2.extdeps.languages.wasm` `wasm_target_model`)"), gunbc.plans.md_helpers.cell(text: "bar-c green + frontier row `self-host: N/A` — **blocked on configuring the runtime row**"), gunbc.plans.md_helpers.cell(text: "configure the `wasmtime` runtime row"), gunbc.plans.md_helpers.cell(text: "emit-generality (stack machine)")]),
        gunbc.plans.md_helpers.row(cells: [gunbc.plans.md_helpers.cell(text: "**machine_code / ptx**"), gunbc.plans.md_helpers.cell(text: "ISA/GPU"), gunbc.plans.md_helpers.cell(text: "**below bar-a** — type model + anchor, **no committed TargetModel** (0 `target_model` / `translation_rules_node` refs)"), gunbc.plans.md_helpers.cell(text: "bar-c green + frontier row `self-host: N/A`, once a TargetModel is built"), gunbc.plans.md_helpers.cell(text: "committed TargetModel, configure the assembler/`ptxas` runtime row"), gunbc.plans.md_helpers.cell(text: "emit-generality (ISA)")]),
      ],
    },
    gunbc.plans.md_helpers.hr(),
    gunbc.plans.md_helpers.h2(text: "Sequencing — Rust-as-model, then stress (dependency-ordered)"),
    gunbc.plans.md_helpers.ul(items: [
      gunbc.plans.md_helpers.li(text: "**Phase A — now-ish (pre-un-shelve):** this map + the `solve` rationale. No emit code. ← *we are here*"),
      gunbc.plans.md_helpers.li(text: "**Phase B — foundation completion (the barrier; everything downstream inherits):** F2 VEP completion (rust + TS). Once B lands, C/D/E run largely in parallel."),
      gunbc.plans.md_helpers.li(text: "**Phase C — self-host axis proof:** generalize F5 past Rust to **Go** (first non-Rust self-host) — and land Rust's own self-host (0/27 today). This is the real \"does the seed-shrink story generalize\" milestone. If it holds, java/kotlin/swift are near-mechanical parallel fan-out."),
      gunbc.plans.md_helpers.li(text: "**Phase D — emit-generality axis (parallel):** Verilog · SPICE · LLVM-IR to bar-c + frontier rows. LLVM-IR still needs a **committed TargetModel**; Verilog's has landed, and SPICE and Verilog have both now been executed by a real tool once, recorded as observations joined to the live emission — what remains for those two is re-execution on a cadence. Each decomposes its `body_lexeme:String` scars and binds its simulator/toolchain transport in a row. This is where the design gets *stressed*; a construct that won't lower produces a typed, located refusal that *names the design gap* — the refusal is the product."),
      gunbc.plans.md_helpers.li(text: "**Phase E — interpreted self-host:** TS → Python (Python inherits TS's VEP completion)."),
      gunbc.plans.md_helpers.li(text: "**Phase F — expression spine:** Lean (falsifies \"is F3 secretly imperative-shaped?\") — first needs its committed TargetModel."),
    ]),
    gunbc.plans.md_helpers.p(text: "Each language is **priced by the design risk it displaces**, not by completeness (§6): Verilog=concurrent, SPICE=continuous, LLVM=SSA/self-host-boundary, Lean=expression-spine. A confirm-only language (java/kotlin/swift) earns its slot only as cheap parallel fan-out after its family's proof lands."),
    gunbc.plans.md_helpers.hr(),
    gunbc.plans.md_helpers.h2(text: "Staffing note (for continuous dispatch)"),
    gunbc.plans.md_helpers.p(text: "Off this map, the natural fan-out is **one child session per language axis**, gated on Phase B. The dependency structure that makes this safe: **B is the only hard barrier** (F2 completion); after it, the self-host axis (C, then the compiled fan-out) and the emit-generality axis (D) have no cross-dependency, so they staff independently. Lean (F) and the interpreted family (E) each ride one Phase-B deliverable (F3-expression-mode and F2-completion respectively) plus their own missing TargetModel where noted. ecmascript's adopt-or-delete decision is a prerequisite gate on the interpreted family, not parallel work."),
  ]
}

data language_target_self_host_frontier_plan: gunbc.plan.Plan = gunbc.plan.Plan {
  slug: "language-target-self-host-frontier",
  title: "Language-target self-host frontier — beginning-to-end dependency map",
  body: language_target_self_host_frontier_body(),
  retirement: gunbc.plan.PlanRetiresWhen { condition: std.dissolution.unbound_dissolution(description: "**Un-shelve is an operator decision (ROADMAP §4 → §1/§3 by PR, priced in displaced cost).** When it fires, this doc + the solve doc are the lane's charter; the typed `LanguageTargetFrontierRow` carrier + completeness/RED witnesses are authored (they do not exist today), the frontier table rows migrate onto per-target carrier rows, the OFFLINE C/Rust F5 smokes are enrolled, and this file dissolves.")
  }
}
